  "final_message": "If you don't pass `max_attempts`, `call_with_retry()` makes at most **4** attempts, counting the first try.\n\n- In `retry.py`, a missing `max_attempts` (`None`) falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`. The function then loops `range(attempts)`, calling `fn()` up to 4 times. It returns on the first success, or re-raises the last exception after the 4th failure.\n- `main7.py` calls `call_with_retry(lambda: 1)` without `max_attempts`, so it uses that default.\n- `MAX_RETRIES = 3` in `decoy_network.py` and `RETRY_LIMIT = 5` in `decoy_backoff.py` don't affect the answer, because `retry.py` doesn't import either one.\n- `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` holds only an empty bundle config and has nothing to do with retries.\n\nANSWER: 4",
